Table full name: bigquery-public-data.nhtsa_traffic_fatalities. accident_2016
Column name: state_number Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the state in which the crash occurred. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). For more info on the codes, please look at <C1/V1/D1/PC1/P1/NM1 State Number> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: state_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies the state in which the crash occurred. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC).
Column name: consecutive_number Type: INT64 Description: This data element is the unique case number assigned to each crash. It appears on each data file and is used to merge information from the data files together. xxxxxx Two Characters for State Code followed by Four Characters for Case Number
Column name: number_of_vehicle_forms_submitted_all Type: INT64 Description: number_of_vehicle_forms_submitted_all
Column name: number_of_motor_vehicles_in_transport_mvit Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of vehicles in-transport involved in the crash. Legally parked vehicles are not included. 001-999 Number of Vehicle Forms
Column name: number_of_parked_working_vehicles Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of parked and working vehicles involved in the crash. 0-999 Number of Parked/Working Vehicles in the Crash
Column name: number_of_forms_submitted_for_persons_not_in_motor_vehicles Type: INT64 Description: This data element is the number of Person Forms (Not a Motor Vehicle Occupant) that are applicable to this case (i.e., non-occupants). 00-99 Number of Persons Not in Motor Vehicles
Column name: number_of_forms_submitted_for_persons_in_motor_vehicles Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of Person Level (Motor Vehicle Occupant) Forms that are applicable to this case (i.e., occupants). 000-999 Number of Person Forms
Column name: number_of_persons_in_motor_vehicles_in_transport_mvit Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of motorists in the crash. A motorist is a driver, passenger or unknown occupant type of a motor vehicle in-transport. 0-999 Number of Persons in Motor Vehicles In-Transport
Column name: number_of_persons_not_in_motor_vehicles_in_transport_mvit Type: INT64 Description: This data element is a count of the number of non-motorists in the crash. A non-motorist is defined as a pedestrian, a cyclist, an occupant of a motor vehicle not intransport, a person riding a horse, an occupant of an animal drawn conveyance, person associated with non-motorist conveyance (e.g., baby carriage, skate board, wheelchair), or an other non-motorist (e.g., person outside a trafficway, person in a house). 0-98 Number of Persons Not in Motor Vehicles in Transport
Column name: county Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the location of the unstabilized event with regard to the County. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). 000 Not Applicable 001-996 Use GSA Geographical Codes 997 Other 998 Not Reported 999 Unknown
Column name: county_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the location of the unstabilized event with regard to the County. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). 000 Not Applicable 001-996 Use GSA Geographical Codes 997 Other 998 Not Reported 999 Unknown
Column name: city Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the location of the unstabilized event with regard to the City. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). 0000 Not Applicable 0001-9996 GSA Geographical Codes 9997 Other 9898 Not Reported 9999 Unknown
Column name: city_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the location of the unstabilized event with regard to the City. The codes are from the General Services Administration’s (GSA) publication of worldwide Geographic Location Codes (GLC). 0000 Not Applicable 0001-9996 GSA Geographical Codes 9997 Other 9898 Not Reported 9999 Unknown
Column name: day_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the day of the month on which the crash occurred. 01-31 Day of the Month of the Crash -- Unknown
Column name: day_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the day of the month on which the crash occurred. 01-31 Day of the Month of the Crash -- Unknown
Column name: month_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the month in which the crash occurred. For more info on the codes, please look at <C8A Month of Crash> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: month_of_crash_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the month in which the crash occurred. For more info on the codes, please look at <C8A Month of Crash> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: year_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the year in which the crash occurred. xxxx Year of the Crash
Column name: day_of_week Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the day of the week on which the crash occurred. 1 Sunday 2 Monday 3 Tuesday 4 Wednesday 5 Thursday 6 Friday 7 Saturday -- Unknown
Column name: day_of_week_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the day of the week on which the crash occurred. 1 Sunday 2 Monday 3 Tuesday 4 Wednesday 5 Thursday 6 Friday 7 Saturday -- Unknown
Column name: hour_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-23 Hour -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: hour_of_crash_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-23 Hour -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: minute_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the minutes after the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-59 Minute -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: minute_of_crash_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the minutes after the hour at which the crash occurred. 00-59 Minute -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: national_highway_system Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies whether this crash occurred on a trafficway that is part of the National Highway System. 0 This Section is Not on the National Highway System 1 This Section is on the National Highway System 9 Unknown
Column name: national_highway_system_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies whether this crash occurred on a trafficway that is part of the National Highway System. 0 This Section is Not on the National Highway System 1 This Section is on the National Highway System 9 Unknown
Column name: route_signing Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the route signing of the trafficway on which the crash occurred. 1 Interstate 2 U.S. Highway 3 State Highway 4 County Road 5 Local Street – Township 6 Local Street – Municipality 7 Local Street – Frontage Road (Since 1994) 8 Other 9 Unknown
Column name: route_signing_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies the route signing of the trafficway on which the crash occurred.
Column name: trafficway_identifier Type: STRING Description: This data element records the trafficway on which the crash occurred. xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx Actual Posted Number, Assigned Number, or Common Name (30 characters) 999999999999999999999999999999 Unknown
Column name: trafficway_identifier_2 Type: STRING Description: This data element records the trafficway on which the crash occurred. xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx Actual Posted Number, Assigned Number, or Common Name (30 characters) 999999999999999999999999999999 Unknown
Column name: land_use Type: INT64 Description: 1 (Rural), 2 (Urban), 6 (Trafficway Not in State Inventory), 8 (Not Reported) and 9 (Unknown).
Column name: land_use_name Type: STRING Description: 1 (Rural), 2 (Urban), 6 (Trafficway Not in State Inventory), 8 (Not Reported) and 9 (Unknown).
Column name: functional_system Type: INT64 Description: 01 (Interstate), 02 (Principal Arterial – Other Freeways and Expressways), 03 (Principal Arterial – Other), 04 (Minor Arterial), 05 (Major Collector), 06 (Minor Collector), 07 (Local), 96 (Trafficway Not in State Inventory), 98 (Not Reported), and 99 (Unknown).
Column name: functional_system_name Type: STRING Description: 01 (Interstate), 02 (Principal Arterial – Other Freeways and Expressways), 03 (Principal Arterial – Other), 04 (Minor Arterial), 05 (Major Collector), 06 (Minor Collector), 07 (Local), 96 (Trafficway Not in State Inventory), 98 (Not Reported), and 99 (Unknown).
Column name: ownership Type: INT64 Description: For more info on the codes, please look at <C13 Ownership> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: ownership_name Type: STRING Description: For more info on the codes, please look at <C13 Ownership> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: milepoint Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the milepoint nearest to the location where the crash occurred. 00000 None xxxxx Actual to Nearest Tenth Mile (Assume decimal, e.g., 12345 = 1234.5) 99998 Not Reported 99999 Unknown
Column name: milepoint_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the milepoint nearest to the location where the crash occurred. 00000 None xxxxx Actual to Nearest Tenth Mile (Assume decimal, e.g., 12345 = 1234.5) 99998 Not Reported 99999 Unknown
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: This element identifies the location of the crash using Global Position coordinates. This is the position of latitude. DDDDDD (DD.DDDD – Decimal Degrees) DD.DDDD Actual Degrees 77.7777 Not Reported 88.8888 Not Available (If State Exempt) 99.9999 Unknown
Column name: latitude_name Type: STRING Description: This element identifies the location of the crash using Global Position coordinates. This is the position of latitude. DDDDDD (DD.DDDD – Decimal Degrees) DD.DDDD Actual Degrees 77.7777 Not Reported 88.8888 Not Available (If State Exempt) 99.9999 Unknown
Column name: longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: This element identifies the location of the crash using Global Position coordinates. This is the position of longitude. DDDDDDD (DDD.DDDD – Decimal Degrees) DDD.DDDD Actual Degrees 777.7777 Not Reported 888.8888 Not Available (If State Exempt) 999.9999 Unknown
Column name: longitude_name Type: STRING Description: This element identifies the location of the crash using Global Position coordinates. This is the position of longitude. DDDDDDD (DDD.DDDD – Decimal Degrees) DDD.DDDD Actual Degrees 777.7777 Not Reported 888.8888 Not Available (If State Exempt) 999.9999 Unknown
Column name: special_jurisdiction Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies if the location on the trafficway where the crash occurred qualifies as a Special Jurisdiction even though it may be patrolled by state, county or local police (e.g., all State highways running through Indian reservations are under the jurisdiction of the Indian reservation). 0 No Special Jurisdiction (Includes National Forests Since 2008) 1 National Park Service 2 Military 3 Indian Reservation 4 College/University Campus 5 Other Federal Properties (Since 1977) 8 Other (Since 1976) 9 Unknown
Column name: special_jurisdiction_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies if the location on the trafficway where the crash occurred qualifies as a Special Jurisdiction even though it may be patrolled by state, county or local police (e.g., all State highways running through Indian reservations are under the jurisdiction of the Indian reservation).
Column name: first_harmful_event Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the first injury or damage producing event of the crash. For more info on the codes, please look at <C19 First Harmful Event> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: first_harmful_event_name Type: STRING Description: This data element describes the first injury or damage producing event of the crash.
Column name: manner_of_collision Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the orientation of two motor vehicles in-transport when they are involved in the “First Harmful Event” of a collision crash. If the “First Harmful Event” is not a collision between two motor vehicles in-transport it is classified as such. For more info on the codes, please look at <C20 Manner of Collision> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: manner_of_collision_name Type: STRING Description: This data element describes the orientation of two motor vehicles in-transport when they are involved in the “First Harmful Event” of a collision crash. If the “First Harmful Event” is not a collision between two motor vehicles in-transport it is classified as such.
Column name: relation_to_junction_within_interchange_area Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the crash's location with respect to presence in an interchange area. The coding of this data element is done in two sub-fields (see also C20B) and is based on the location of the “First Harmful Event” of the crash. 0 No 1 Yes 8 Not Reported 9 Unknown
Column name: relation_to_junction_within_interchange_area_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies the crash's location with respect to presence in an interchange area. The coding of this data element is done in two sub-fields (see also C20B) and is based on the location of the “First Harmful Event” of the crash. 0 No 1 Yes 8 Not Reported 9 Unknown
Column name: relation_to_junction_specific_location Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the crash's location with respect to presence in or proximity to components typically in junction or interchange areas. The coding of this data element is done in two sub-fields (see also C20A) and is based on the location of the “First Harmful Event” of the crash. For more info on the codes, please look at <C21B Relation to Junction- Specific Location> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: relation_to_junction_specific_location_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies the crash's location with respect to presence in or proximity to components typically in junction or interchange areas. The coding of this data element is done in two sub-fields (see also C20A) and is based on the location of the “First Harmful Event” of the crash.
Column name: type_of_intersection Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies and allows separation of various intersection types. 1 Not an Intersection 2 Four-Way Intersection 3 T-Intersection 4 Y-Intersection 5 Traffic Circle 6 Roundabout 7 Five-Point, or More 10 L-Intersection 98 Not Reported 99 Unknown
Column name: type_of_intersection_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies and allows separation of various intersection types. 1 Not an Intersection 2 Four-Way Intersection 3 T-Intersection 4 Y-Intersection 5 Traffic Circle 6 Roundabout 7 Five-Point, or More 10 L-Intersection 98 Not Reported 99 Unknown
Column name: work_zone Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies a motor vehicle traffic crash in which the first harmful event occurs within the boundaries of a work zone or on an approach to or exit from a work zone, resulting from an activity, behavior, or control related to the movement of the traffic units through the work zone. 0 None 1 Construction 2 Maintenance -- Construction or Maintenance 3 Utility 4 Work Zone, Type Unknown -- Not Reported
Column name: work_zone_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies a motor vehicle traffic crash in which the first harmful event occurs within the boundaries of a work zone or on an approach to or exit from a work zone, resulting from an activity, behavior, or control related to the movement of the traffic units through the work zone. 0 None 1 Construction 2 Maintenance -- Construction or Maintenance 3 Utility 4 Work Zone, Type Unknown -- Not Reported
Column name: relation_to_trafficway Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the location of the crash as it relates to its position within or outside the trafficway based on the “First Harmful Event.” For more info on the codes, please look at <C23 Relation to Trafficway> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: relation_to_trafficway_name Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies the location of the crash as it relates to its position within or outside the trafficway based on the “First Harmful Event.”
Column name: light_condition Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the type/level of light that existed at the time of the crash as indicated in the case material. For more info on the codes, please look at <C25 Light Condition> section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: light_condition_name Type: STRING Description: This data element records the type/level of light that existed at the time of the crash as indicated in the case material.
